<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I52d269a57e7b30159af25a1a1a979c285d319b46" commit="3cb78351f41fb7113b374eef19206cc24a5132a3" commit_message="Install touch seccomp policies per-architecture  Previously there was only 1 set of seccomp policies for the touch firmware updater scripts, but now we have some of these devices on multiple architectures.  As a result, they use different syscalls if they're on arm, vs x86, etc so the policies to carry over. This CL changes the ebuild to pull policies from a directory named with the architecture in question.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:60015 TEST=emerged and deployed touch_updater on several systems that use these seccomp policies on different architectures.  The policies are pulled from the right directories and work smoothly CQ-DEPEND=CL:412322  Change-Id: I52d269a57e7b30159af25a1a1a979c285d319b46 Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/412340 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jorge Lucangeli Obes &lt;jorgelo@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="412340" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/40/412340/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I987ec538dcd810b16f76a4381e17737a78076c53" commit="8b65604a81eadae565a3216a528dc8b26527183d" commit_message="Set up arch-depended seccomp policies  Depending on the architecture, systems will need different seccomp policies to run their various touch firmware updaters.  Previously we didn't account for this, so this CL adds architecture directories that contain the policies that correspond to that arch.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:60015 TEST=manually deployed and tested on several different architectures and DUTS. CQ-DEPEND=CL:412340  Change-Id: I987ec538dcd810b16f76a4381e17737a78076c53 Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/412322 Reviewed-by: Dennis Kempin &lt;denniskempin@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Jorge Lucangeli Obes &lt;jorgelo@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="412322" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" ref="refs/changes/22/412322/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ied4a9f93a4d44714c012d3a3e50e4a34f41a7c1f" commit="8b8091d9ac3750386aa647704c6fe4edacfc6863" commit_message="ISH: set toolchain in core/minute-ia  When &quot;make buildall&quot; has board which uses core/minute-ia, CROSS_COMPILE?=i686-pc-linux-gnu- doesn't get set unless CROSS_COMPILE is not defined; however, it's defined before this line, and wrong toolchain is used. Remove &quot;?&quot; to set correct CROSS_COMPILE.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST='make buildall -j' passed  Change-Id: Ied4a9f93a4d44714c012d3a3e50e4a34f41a7c1f Signed-off-by: li feng &lt;li1.feng@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/410402 Commit-Ready: Li1 Feng &lt;li1.feng@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Li1 Feng &lt;li1.feng@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="410402" owner_email="li1.feng@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/02/410402/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia80232da42aa705df819a4988da483a344ffcbb4" commit="e3a2ccd6b2bdce8bc6fb59a88b1d3dc8cb66275a" commit_message="driver: bmi160: Remove unnecessary delay  Rereading the specification, remove delays when not needed: - When we move the sensor out of suspend, we need to wait before using it (BMI160 spec: 2.11.38 Register (0x7E) CMD) When we do a softreset, we need just need to wait 300us for the sensor to go in suspend, we will wait only when we change the rate and enable the sensor. - The timeout at fifo flush is not needed, it was added for debugging. - Remove unnecessary printf when initializing the magnetometer.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:59188 BRANCH=glados, reef, strago TEST=On reef, check the EC boot faster: time spend initializing the sensors decreased from 240ms to 133ms  Change-Id: Ia80232da42aa705df819a4988da483a344ffcbb4 Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/411964 Commit-Ready: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="411964" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/64/411964/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4092f049473fe46fc31dab85a44d206402417c7b" commit="cfdbc0ead3d8b0e1564d860a8a23b7f0dec2d5df" commit_message="netifaces: upgraded package to upstream  Upgraded dev-python/netifaces to version 0.10.5 on amd64  BUG=None TEST=Tested locally on a Guado box, which uses netifaces for ip address checking.  Change-Id: I4092f049473fe46fc31dab85a44d206402417c7b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/411450 Commit-Ready: Chunxiao Diao &lt;cdiao@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Chunxiao Diao &lt;cdiao@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="411450" owner_email="cdiao@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/portage-stable" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/portage-stable" ref="refs/changes/50/411450/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id6c4adf1fc055bfeace26cb236a0b23c833e19cd" commit="11201231ef0a591bad4d38b7010b39c0add7a0d8" commit_message="autotest: retry staging when devserver returns invalid response.  There's a case that when devserver is overloaded and cannot handle some requests like 'stage', it will return invalid responses, which won't be raised as an HTTP error and leads to stage process terminated.  This CL retry such cases. When invalid response is detected, stage will be retried after 30 seconds to 1) not add more burden on that devserver, 2) make stage process continue, not be terminated.  BUG=chromium:615650 TEST=Locally run ds.trigger_download() with devserver, test whether it's retried when the returned response of devserver is invalid.  Change-Id: Id6c4adf1fc055bfeace26cb236a0b23c833e19cd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/412150 Commit-Ready: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="412150" owner_email="xixuan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/50/412150/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I45d333847843f37048927a2cca273327f28adad8" commit="08bb81e5ec5a178706bbcc0dc45eb10ac207ae18" commit_message="Devserver: logging all errors in extracting tarball.  This CL separates the stdout and stderr of command 'tar', and log the error message if stderr is not empty.  BUG=chromium:659850 TEST=Create a future file, tar -czvf it, and then call common_util.ExtractTarball to verify.  Change-Id: I45d333847843f37048927a2cca273327f28adad8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/412305 Commit-Ready: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="412305" owner_email="xixuan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/dev-util" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/dev-util" ref="refs/changes/05/412305/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie9bd0a5f9bf73562ed5b56a0f415fdff9b72098d" commit="d291f677737dbd70f7702394b8819d1286c40868" commit_message="net-wireless/bluez: Add bluetoothd option in upstart script  bluetoothd has several built-in profiles by default. Some platform may need to disable some of them, such as Google WiFi AP (Gale) need to disable AVRCP. Variable BLUETOOTH_DAEMON_OPTION is added in upstart script for this. By default it is emoty, can be set by installing bluetoothd.override into /etc/init by board-specific overlay.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:58573 TEST=Build image for gale, check SDP record  Change-Id: Ie9bd0a5f9bf73562ed5b56a0f415fdff9b72098d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/409551 Commit-Ready: Yuji Sasaki &lt;sasakiy@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Yuji Sasaki &lt;sasakiy@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Yuji Sasaki &lt;sasakiy@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="409551" owner_email="sasakiy@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/51/409551/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icafbdc3cf66521b82a37fbf978c67f43561a561e" commit="828400f40a4c59172b094f8d255c7fd9baecab48" commit_message="container_utils: devices are optional in OCI config  If the devices section is missing from the OCI configuration don't fail, it isn't a hard requirement.  Containers are allowed to run without any devices.  BUG=none TEST=updated container_config_parser_unittest  Change-Id: Icafbdc3cf66521b82a37fbf978c67f43561a561e Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/410702 Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="410702" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/02/410702/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4710706eb62948f7079b79fdc07bc576c4ee9831" commit="216be138ffbf07dd17b3f038b21212261535af95" commit_message="Save SDK_TOOLS artifacts to a public GS location  The adb/aapt tools can be distributed publicly.  BUG=b:32840163 TEST=None  Change-Id: I4710706eb62948f7079b79fdc07bc576c4ee9831 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/410228 Commit-Ready: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="410228" owner_email="bhthompson@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/28/410228/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><lkgm version="9011.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>